    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe registration-date business-day rule lived in `BusinessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/BusinessDayAdjuster.java`), called from `OwnerRestControllerV1.effectiveRegistrationDate(...)`. It only rolled Saturdays/Sundays forward to Monday and returned a public holiday unchanged \u2014 so a registration date landing on a listed holiday was not adjusted.\n\nI extended it to also skip the fixed public-holiday list:\n\n- Added `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS = {2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28}`.\n- Replaced the fixed weekend jumps with a roll-forward loop (`plusDays(1)`) that continues while the date is a weekend **or** a public holiday, landing on the next non-holiday business day. This correctly chains cases like 2026-12-25 (Fri holiday) \u2192 26 (Sat) \u2192 27 (Sun) \u2192 28 (Mon holiday) \u2192 29 (Tue).\n\nThis mirrors the reference logic already in the test harness (`AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay` with the same `HOLIDAYS` set).\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` holiday/business-day invariant passes).",
